{
  "slug": "interview-prep-toolkit",
  "title": "Interview Prep Toolkit",
  "subtitle": "Structure, Stories, and Strategies to Win Every Interview",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Why Interview Prep Matters",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "The best candidates often don’t get offers—not because they lack skills, but because they fail to **communicate effectively.** An interview is not just Q&A; it’s a **persuasion exercise.**"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Employers ask:"
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "Can this person do the job? (skills)",
            "Will they fit into the culture? (values)",
            "Do I want to work with them daily? (presence)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Reflection",
          "text": "Think of your last interview. Did you answer to impress or just to respond?",
          "lines": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Understand Recruiter Psychology",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Recruiters don’t have time to dig. They want:"
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "**Clarity:** Simple, direct answers.",
            "**Confidence:** No overthinking.",
            "**Consistency:** Stories aligned across resume, LinkedIn, and answers."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "Write 3 adjectives you want an interviewer to remember about you (e.g., analytical, collaborative, resilient).",
          "lines": 4,
          "numbered": 3
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 1"
    },
    {
      "title": "Researching the Company & Role",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Interviewers expect you to know **why them.**"
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "Study company strategy (annual reports, press releases).",
            "Know recent deals/initiatives.",
            "Understand role expectations (JD keywords)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "Write one reason you want this company specifically—not generic.",
          "lines": 3
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 2"
    },
    {
      "title": "Crafting Your Personal Pitch",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "“Tell me about yourself” = your pitch moment. Keep it **2 minutes, structured, confident.**"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Framework: Past → Present → Future."
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "Past: Background.",
            "Present: Current role/strengths.",
            "Future: Why this role/company."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "Write your 2-minute pitch in 3–4 bullet points.",
          "lines": 4,
          "table": {
            "columns": [
              "",
              "My pitch"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Past",
                ""
              ],
              [
                "Present",
                ""
              ],
              [
                "Future",
                ""
              ],
              [
                "Why this role",
                ""
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 3"
    },
    {
      "title": "Mastering Behavioral Questions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Common Qs:"
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "“Tell me about a time you led a team.”",
            "“Tell me about a conflict.”",
            "“Describe a failure.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Always use STAR (Situation, Task, Action, Result)."
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "Write 1 STAR story for leadership.",
          "lines": 4,
          "table": {
            "columns": [
              "",
              "My leadership story"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Situation",
                ""
              ],
              [
                "Task",
                ""
              ],
              [
                "Action",
                ""
              ],
              [
                "Result",
                ""
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 4"
    },
    {
      "title": "Building a STAR Story Bank",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Don’t prepare 2–3 stories. Prepare **10–12 across themes**: leadership, problem-solving, teamwork, resilience, innovation."
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Worksheet",
          "text": "Fill in your story bank: one skill per row and the story that proves it. Aim for at least five.",
          "lines": 4,
          "table": {
            "columns": [
              "Skill",
              "My story (a few words to jog your memory)"
            ],
            "rows": 8
          }
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 5"
    },
    {
      "title": "Handling Strengths & Weaknesses Questions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "**Strengths:** Link to role (e.g., “analytical thinking” for consulting).",
            "**Weaknesses:** Be honest but show improvement."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Example Weakness: “I used to overanalyze, but I now use structured decision-making to balance speed and accuracy.”"
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "Write 1 strength + 1 weakness aligned to your target role.",
          "lines": 4,
          "table": {
            "columns": [
              "",
              "Mine, linked to the role"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Strength",
                ""
              ],
              [
                "Weakness and how I’m improving",
                ""
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 6"
    },
    {
      "title": "Preparing for Technical/Role-Specific Questions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Consulting → case studies, profitability math.",
            "Finance → valuation, ratios, DCF.",
            "Tech → coding basics, product thinking."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "Write 3 technical questions you expect in your role.",
          "lines": 4,
          "numbered": 3
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 7"
    },
    {
      "title": "Asking Smart Questions to Interviewers",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "End with strong questions—it shows curiosity and fit."
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "“What skills make someone excel in this role here?”",
            "“How does this team contribute to the company’s growth strategy?”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "avoid",
          "items": [
            "Don’t ask about salary at first round."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "Write 2 smart questions you’ll ask in your next interview.",
          "lines": 4,
          "numbered": 2
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 8"
    },
    {
      "title": "Mock Interviews & Practice Strategies",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Practice is the difference. Options:"
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "Peer practice.",
            "Mock interviews with mentors.",
            "AI-based interview tools."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "Schedule 1 mock interview this week.",
          "lines": 2
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 9"
    },
    {
      "title": "Cracking a consulting interview",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Megha practised 40+ cases with peers, refined her STAR stories and rehearsed with a mentor. Result: a business analyst offer from a strategy firm.",
            "Lesson: **Consistency beats cramming.**"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "example": true
    },
    {
      "title": "Cracking a finance interview",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Rohit used targeted resume bullets, practised 50+ finance technical questions and built strong why-finance answers. Result: an investment banking offer.",
            "Lesson: **Alignment + confidence win finance interviews.**"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "example": true
    },
    {
      "title": "Common Mistakes and Your 90-Day Plan",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Mistakes: Winging answers, ignoring PEI, no prep for technicals.",
            "Fix: Story bank, mocks, research."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "plan",
          "rows": [
            [
              "Weeks 1–4",
              "Build STAR story bank."
            ],
            [
              "Weeks 5–8",
              "Practice technicals."
            ],
            [
              "Weeks 9–12",
              "Mock interviews + refine pitch."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
